{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487519-first-change","id":487519,"title":"First Change","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-21T12:47:13-07:00","id":487519,"title":"First Change","content":"I know the First Change is a mysterious process that can happen to a person or wolf-blood out of the blue. It has no specific way into doing it. Though I was thinking, can Lunacy be use to trigger the First Change as well? I know lunacy can make wolf-bloods through dramatic failures and gain a bonus if victim is wounded; that kind of sounds like how I did it when I played 1ed and turn mortal characters into Uratha through damage (bite &amp; scratch).<br /> <br /> Just curious. How did you make your characters go through the First Change?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T14:57:58-07:00","id":487654,"title":"","content":"2e actually has a system if you want to play out a wolf-blooded going through the First Change. It involves gaining points of Tension and once Tension reaches 10, boom!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T15:37:56-07:00","id":487721,"title":"","content":"I'd suggest that if a mortal has the potential, and sustains a wound from a Uratha in Gauru form while in <i>kuruth</i> or on the <i>Siskur-Dah</i>, that should almost certainly qualify as a trigger for the first change, as well as death rage itself. While Lunacy is probably as good a cause as any, there's still some sort of psyche trying to preserve some constructed reality, whereas tasting utter destruction at the hands of a rampaging death machine should remove any and all shackles of sanity and rationality, thus allowing the spirit-wolf inside to react freely. It also does make the Iron Masters absolutely right that Man is the most dangerous prey, because they're full of unsuspected Death Raging Werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T16:48:22-07:00","id":487794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanandithras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487519-first-change?p=487654#post487654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e actually has a system if you want to play out a wolf-blooded going through the First Change. It involves gaining points of Tension and once Tension reaches 10, boom!</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, I must have miss that. What page is it on? (I haven't read the whole book, yet.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T18:02:34-07:00","id":487823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487519-first-change?p=487794#post487794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really, I must have miss that. What page is it on? (I haven't read the whole book, yet.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Starts on page 291, begins with a section called &quot;The First Change Story&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T18:13:59-07:00","id":487826,"title":"","content":"I wonder how capable a wolf blooded &quot;in the know&quot; would be of recognizing when they are going through the first change? I mean, if a wolf-blood had been part of a pack theit whole life and knew what the signs of the first change were and had a room capable of holding a werewolf prepared for just the occasion, would that wolf-blood be able to lock himself up so that they didn't hurt anyone during the first change?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T19:10:28-07:00","id":487844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487519-first-change?p=487826#post487826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how capable a wolf blooded &quot;in the know&quot; would be of recognizing when they are going through the first change? I mean, if a wolf-blood had been part of a pack theit whole life and knew what the signs of the first change were and had a room capable of holding a werewolf prepared for just the occasion, would that wolf-blood be able to lock himself up so that they didn't hurt anyone during the first change?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would depend on how violently the first Rage came on, I think. If there was enough stress and a traumatic event, it could happen in a flash of blood and whirling claws. If it was more of a slow burn, the wolf-blood might have time if they can fight it off until a great, vicious release (Res+Comp?).<br /> <br /> They might recognize the signs in the first few weeks (the more knowledgeable ones, that is), but they could also play it off as just feeling ill or under the weather. There's also those that could be paranoid they will change; in one of the 1e books, a wolf-blooded is locked out without much food or water by their family because the family is SURE that they will change eventually. The text ends on a rather grim note, with the implication that the wolf-blood might be left down there to starve out of fear by their relatives (I think).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}